{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213907,"nonce":"rx3sDyMzFkhHq5c/rUCAI1zIPqE=","title":"krio-fiber backing on by default for AOT and JIT; retire the stackless SM transform on native","message":"Depends on conservative stack scanning (suspended krio stacks become roots by scan). Supersedes the older opt-in issue once landed.\n\n- One scheduler per OS thread in TLS; VmFiber { Box\u003cFiber\u003e, id, run_state Runnable|Running|Waiting(token), resume_cause, per-fiber trap/exception state }.\n- Wait tokens in a global registry with claim-then-deliver (claim_notification / claim_timeout) so stale timers and duplicate wakes are harmless; timers as a min-heap; sleep on a fiber is a timer park, never a thread sleep.\n- schedule_step records the main stack's sp for the GC before resuming and publishes fiber.saved_sp() immediately after the fiber yields, before any hook that can collect.\n- Epoch-word safepoint: AtomicU64 bumped only when something needs attention (mailbox push, fiber creation, GC stop, 2 ms timer thread); compiled loops compare a per-activation cached epoch and call a cold poll helper; Cranelift uses a plain aligned load.\n- 256 KiB mmap stacks with a guard page (krio), charged to GC external pressure.\n\n- Flip WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER default to on for native; Fiber.yield/try/transfer switch synchronously from any depth, so JIT'd and AOT bodies no longer need to stay in the bytecode interpreter (closes the JIT-cannot-suspend issue for native).\n- Delete transform_to_state_machine, compute_aot_tainted_method_names, BlockKind, aot_frames, aot_active_depth, the CrossFnCallInit/Resume split, the Mechanism B Yield arm, and WLIFT_AOT_CALL_N.\n- Loop-header safepoint polls in Cranelift and AOT so a hot loop yields to a timer-driven scheduler and reaches the collector.\n\nFull hatch spec corpus (41) and hatch/site under AOT and tiered with krio on; compare against the SM path before deleting it.","files":null}]}